@using CoupleOS.Application.Capture
@model SharedFileView

@*
    The other partner saved while this one was typing.

    ADR 0009 settles this as last-write-wins with a stale-version warning, and
    the warning is the whole of the mechanism: nothing is locked, nothing is
    merged, and pressing Save again will overwrite what is shown below — the
    version input has already moved on, so the second press succeeds. That is
    deliberate. What is refused is the silent overwrite, not the overwrite.

    Their text is rendered here rather than summarised, because the decision the
    user is about to make is whether to replace it, and nobody can make that
    decision from a count of lines.
*@

<p class="warning">
    Not saved — your partner saved version @Model.Version while you were typing.
    Your text is still in the box. Press Save again to replace theirs with yours.
</p>

<details>
    <summary>What they wrote</summary>
    <pre class="their-copy">@Model.Content</pre>
</details>
